WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.300
One of the things we talk about is the
best Spider-Man stories are when Peter

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.020
and Spider-Man's worlds collide.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.280
It's been a thrill working on Spider-Man for the first time

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:17.500
and doing it with our longtime partners at Playstation or Sony Interactive Entertainment.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.020
Spider-man is a character that is super

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:25.980
beloved by many people and Insomniac
myself included and we also know that he

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.220
has millions of fans around the world, he's
one of the most beloved characters

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:36.930
of all of media period so we felt a lot
of responsibility to try and make a

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:42.660
great experience for players, but
focus really hard on bringing you a kind

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:48.329
of a fresh Spider-Man experience that
respects the DNA of the series and feels

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:53.430
right but also will surprise you in new
ways and it starts with the fact that

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:57.210
this is not an origin story this is not
based on a comic or a movie,

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:02.399
it's a brand new experience starting a 23-year-old Peter Parker who is masterful at

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:06.840
fighting crime and it's gonna have some
great personal relationships.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.420
You're gonna see the Peter's side of it and
you're also going to see the Spider-Man side.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.290
I don't think it was really hard
to decide that we wanted to, you know,

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:19.060
take the best things and our favorite
things from past Spider-Man comics and lore.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.480
There's so much good stuff over decades, you have all these great

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:28.950
characters and Spider-Man has been in so
many different situations and bought so

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.850
many villains and fans have many
favorite moments and so we wanted to

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:37.500
honor that legacy and try and do things
that we as fans would want to see while

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.640
also providing a lot of Easter eggs for
fans as well.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.440
But we weren't just thinking it had to be all classic,

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.040
I mean, if you look at the choice of Mr Negative,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.940
he's a very modern Spider-Man villain

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.140
Dan Slott created him I think nine years
ago, maybe 10 now, so he's relatively

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:57.140
newcomer and if you haven't been keeping
up with the comics, you may have no idea who he is,

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.940
so it's great to bring him to
potentially his largest audience yet.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.100
It was really important to us to
tell a story that we wanted to tell.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.599
We have amazing ideas, we love Spider-Man,
and as fans if we were gonna sit down

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:13.430
and play like a new
big Spider-Man game, we would want

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:17.990
something that would, you know, feel like
very much like Spider-Man, but at the

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:23.600
same time, be surprising and so it was
kind of just us knowing that if we were

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.160
gonna play this game, it's what we would
want.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.580
Creating a 23-year-old Peter Parker
allowed us a lot of things.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.900
that we couldn't have gotten with a 15-year-old one.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.720
Firstly, he's already great at
fighting crimes so we can let players be

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.740
awesome at being Spider-Man.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:44.220
This isn't a game where he's trying to learn his powers
and figure out how to web-swing

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:48.060
and not being good at fighting guys, we can throw you right into the deep end

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:53.980
into some crazy situations because you are a masterful Spider-Man who's been Spider-Man for eight years.

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:58.070
On top of that, there's sort of high
school relationships that you have that

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:01.800
the classic 15-year-old Peter Parker
explores.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.700
we wanted to sort of explore what your
relationships are and what your life is

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:11.820
like after you get out of university and
you start a job while also trying to be a superhero.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.060
A classic thing about Spider-Man is

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:19.970
how to handle the next step of life and
that's something that Peter always has

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:23.640
dealt with whether he's been in high
school or he's in college.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.740
We're just doing that for what it's like when you
finally are an adult.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:32.120
Well, New York is this like melting pot of cultures so we
wanted to reflect that as accurately as

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.340
we could and there's kind of a very
large Chinatown district.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.200
We wanted these characters to still be very authentic to
who they were, like just because our

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.820
Peter Parker is 23 years old, he still
should act and feel like Peter Parker

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.900
and maybe people are wearing are in
different jobs, like MJ is a reporter at

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.700
The Daily Bugle or Norman Osborn as the
mayor, but we still want them to be true

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:56.000
to their actual characters and true to
the character traits that have been

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.360
defined for them so that's kind of how
we're blending things and and I think

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:06.050
showing other cultures especially as it
relates to Kingpin or to the city of New

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:11.820
York or to Mr Negative, it's just important to be authentic to their to those characters and that universe.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.320
So we have Marvel's New York, the island of Manhattan,

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.230
after the first mission, you
can just swing around and see the whole

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.610
swing everywhere all the way from
financial district up to Harlem.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.300
We wanted to have a really detailed city
that feels doesn't just look like New

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.219
York but feels like it when you're in it.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.040
This is not a dark abandoned city,

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:34.750
it's got pedestrians and traffic, so
as you explore the city, there will be

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:38.200
additional activities for you to do.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.600
Some of these are little collectibles like 
Peter leaves backpacks everywhere

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.980
when he goes to fight crimes,
 and then he forgets where they are.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:47.000
Each one has like
a different piece of memorabilia, so to

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.320
speak, that kind of tells you a little bit about
the story of his first eight years as Spider-Man

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.020
There's other
collectibles too, like there's landmarks

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:59.689
that Peter can take photos of, there are
stakeouts that Black Cat has been up to

00:04:59.689 --> 00:05:03.780
but then there's also side quests and
some interesting side missions.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.200
It's a big game and it will depend a lot on how
much side content you do but even if you

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:13.520
don't do a lot of the side content, there's still 
a very satisfying and long story there for him.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.340
But one that I really think is interesting and we tried

00:05:15.349 --> 00:05:19.129
to mix and tie the story and everything where
we could, is there are these research

00:05:19.129 --> 00:05:23.960
stations that Harry Osborn set up as a
project to help clean up New York.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:30.380
Now, Harry is currently away - Harry is 
Peter's best friend - in Europe for studying at school,

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:33.720
and so he asked Peter to check in on his research stations for him.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.060
But little does Harry know 
that actually Spider-Man

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.860
is doing the checking in and using some
special web powers to help do the

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.780
the research that Harry was trying to get done.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:48.139
We're huge fans of Spider-Man at Insomniac
so we've been working hard on this for

00:05:48.139 --> 00:05:52.219
over three-and-a-half years, we poured a
lot of energy and effort into it.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:57.460
We're very excited for you all to play the
game, try to avoid spoilers,

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.080
there are a lot of little surprises and big 
surprises still left to be discovered.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.400
and we can't wait for you to play on September 7th!

